cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it as below. The results it reproduces
  are reported in the manuscript listed under references.
title: "IC_Grafos_FIIs: PMFG and MST portfolio selection for Brazilian real estate investment funds"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jang"
    given-names: "Yoon Sung"
    affiliation: "School of Technology (FT), University of Campinas (UNICAMP)"
  - family-names: "Carneiro da Silva"
    given-names: "Augusto"
    affiliation: "School of Technology (FT), University of Campinas (UNICAMP)"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic pipeline that builds Planar Maximally Filtered Graphs (PMFG)
  and Minimum Spanning Trees (MST) from the return correlations of 51
  Brazilian real estate investment funds (FIIs), forms Central, Peripheral
  and Hybrid portfolios by composite centrality, and evaluates them out of
  sample with transaction costs, the 20% capital-gains tax and the CDI as the
  risk-free rate, against the IFIX and classical Markowitz benchmarks. The
  frozen input data are included, and a single run regenerates every table
  and figure of the manuscript.
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoonsungj04/IC_Grafos_FIIs"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - portfolio selection
  - planar maximally filtered graph
  - minimum spanning tree
  - correlation networks
  - real estate investment funds
  - FII
  - econophysics
references:
  - type: unpublished
    title: "A Unified Comparison of Graph-Based Portfolio Construction for Brazilian Real Estate Investment Funds under Realistic Trading Conditions"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Carneiro da Silva"
        given-names: "Augusto"
      - family-names: "Jang"
        given-names: "Yoon Sung"
      - family-names: "Bertini Junior"
        given-names: "João Roberto"
    year: 2026
    notes: "Manuscript in preparation."
